'''Steel dragons''' are the third weakest of the six types of [[metal dragons]]. Like all metal dragons, they can attack from a distance with [[dragonfire]]. Complete protection requires an [[antifire potion]] together with either an [[anti-dragon shield]] or [[dragonfire shield]]. Using only one of these forms of protection reduces, but does not prevent, dragonfire damage. The [[Protect from Magic]] [[prayer]] provides no protection against dragonfire from metal dragons. Alternatively, a [[super antifire potion]] or [[extended super antifire]] provides complete protection without a shield.

[[Magic]] and [[Ranged]] are commonly used against steel dragons because they do not move into [[melee]] range, allowing players with complete dragonfire protection to avoid all damage while attacking from a distance. Magic is particularly effective because steel dragons have a relatively low magic level and a weakness to [[earth spells]].

Melee users should use [[Protect from Melee]], as steel dragons can deal heavy melee damage. Stab weapons, such as the [[Ghrazi rapier]] and [[Osmumten's fang]], are generally more effective than slash or crush weapons because steel dragons have a lower stab defence bonus. [[Dragonbane weapons]], particularly the [[dragon hunter lance]], are also highly effective due to their additional bonuses against [[Draconic (attribute)|draconic creatures]].

Players without complete dragonfire protection should remain in melee range and use protect from melee. This reduces the frequency of dragonfire attacks while preventing damage from the dragons' melee attacks. Melee users with complete dragonfire protection can instead step out of melee range between attacks, returning only to attack the dragon. This avoids its melee attacks and reduces the need to use protect from melee.

After completing the [[Elite Karamja Diary]], players can speak to [[Pirate Jackie the Fruit]] to toggle whether the [[Bronze dragon|bronze]], [[Iron dragon|iron]], and steel dragons in [[Brimhaven Dungeon]] drop their respective metal bars in [[Bank note|noted form]].
